# Universal Entity Sync Standard

Every primary domain entity that is tenant operational truth MUST carry:

- `entity_sync_id` (UUID, UNIQUE, never reused)
- `row_version` (monotonic integer)
- `updated_at` (RFC3339 UTC)
- and MUST stage a typed outbox item on every durable mutation

No business domain may remain a local-only island without:

1. a `SYNC_ENTITY` registry key in `src-tauri/src/sync/domain.rs`
2. a versioned sync payload whose foreign keys are `entity_sync_id` (never local `i64`)
3. an inbox materialization handler that upserts the real domain table

Canonical identity across machines is `entity_sync_id`. Local INTEGER PKs are device-local. Existing columns named `sync_id` MUST be renamed to `entity_sync_id` in the same schema program (no dual-read aliases).

Desktop trusted machines receive the full tenant operational replica. RBAC and org scope are enforced at command/query time on every device — not by omitting rows from desktop sync (that would fork truth). Mobile (later) may use a device-class filter; records that do sync remain byte-compatible with desktop payloads.

Attachments sync as metadata envelopes plus object-store binaries (`tenant/entity_sync_id/content_sha256`). JSON outbox MUST NOT carry file bytes.

Derived caches, sync-control tables, and device-local secrets (PIN, session keyring) are not primary sync entities.

**SSOT:** `docs/engineering/SYNC_STRATEGY.md`

```text
❌ BAD — mutate work_orders without stage_outbox_item
❌ BAD — sync payload with asset_id: 42 (local i64)
❌ BAD — insert sync_inbox with apply_status='applied' without writing domain tables
✅ GOOD — entity_sync_id + row_version + outbox + materializer
✅ GOOD — equipment_entity_sync_id: "<uuid>" in payload; remap to local id on apply
```
